I've just made a significant change to unicorn horns. I know you guys
don't care much, but I just want to ask what you think of this anyway.
(I say 'you don't care' because no one has used the git repository
yet!)

The change is that unicorn horns now need to rest (age, recharge)
between uses to be reliable. The motivation for this change is that I
want status effects to still play some role in the late game, even
though unicorn horns can cure them all in a single turn. I think it's
good that unicorn horns can cure all that stuff instantly, but I think
it's a shame that as soon as you get a unicorn horn, a heap of
interesting elements of the game are essentially removed. Exploding
lights, thrown potions, booby trapped doors, the stun from the new
helm of anti-magic, gaze attacks from umber hulks, and other... all
are effects that are nearly completely negated by having a unicorn
horn =96 thus the game gets simpler as it goes on, and I think that's
the wrong way for it to be. So... I've changed unicorn horns to have a
kind of recharge time so that every time a condition is inflicted on
you, instead of just going straight for the unicorn horn, you need to
make a decision: "is this a trivial conditions that I should just wait
out or is it worth depleting some of my unicorn horn charge?"

I personally think this is a really good change, or at least a good
idea =96 it may take some testing and tweaking to get the balance right.
But I'm not sure that everyone will agree that it's a good idea, and
I'd like to hear what you think. (Janis, thanks for sticking up for
vanilla nethack. Although I usually charge forward with my changes
anyway, I really appreciate hearing the criticisms and
counterarguments.)

For those interested in the details, here is the relevant code:
	// +1% per 20 moves
	// +20% if sick, because sickness is potentially fatal. We don't want
to be too harsh.
	// the total probability is increased by a factor of 100/80 if the
horn is blessed
	val_limit =3D ((moves - obj->age)/20 + (Sick?20 :0) > rn2(100-(obj-
>blessed?20:0)))? 1 : 0;
	if (val_limit > 0)
	{
		// cap at the maximum age.
		obj->age =3D max(moves - 2000, moves - obj->age);
		// use up most of the age.
		obj->age =3D moves - (moves - obj->age)/(obj->blessed?3 :4);

		// check for a bonus cure
		val_limit +=3D ((moves - obj->age)/20 + (Sick?20 :0) > rn2(100-(obj-
>blessed?20:0)))? 1 : 0;
	}

Also, just while I'm posting an update, here's another potentially
interesting change: The bite attack of dragons now has a special
effect for each dragon type. Red: fire, white: cold, blue: electric,
yellow: acid, black: acid as well (disintergration might be a bit too
harsh), orange: paralysis, gray: stun, green: poison, silver: no
special effect.
So watch out. Blue dragons and orange dragons are particularly
dangerous.


